# End-to-end: firstmate home with config/branch-prefix = ardy
# (firstmate checkout at commit 2ca9da4; unrelated live-watcher supervision banners filtered)

## 1. Firstmate scaffolds a local-only brief
$ FM_HOME=/tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/home bin/fm-brief.sh ship-demo-1 <project> --mode local-only
scaffolded: /tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/home/data/ship-demo-1/brief.md (ship, mode=local-only; replace {TASK})
Branch-naming lines from the generated brief (data/ship-demo-1/brief.md):
18:1. First action: create your branch: `git checkout -b ardy/ship-demo-1`
21:1. Never push to any remote and never open a PR. Work only on your `ardy/ship-demo-1` branch; firstmate handles the merge into local `main`.
61:The task is complete only when committed on your branch `ardy/ship-demo-1`. Do NOT push, do NOT open a PR, do NOT merge.
63:When it is implemented and committed, append `done: ready in branch ardy/ship-demo-1` to the status file and stop.

## 2. The crewmate follows the brief: works on ardy/ship-demo-1, reports ready
$ git checkout -b ardy/ship-demo-1 && (edit+commit feature.txt) && git checkout main
status file line: done: ready in branch ardy/ship-demo-1

## 3. Firstmate records the task meta, then reviews the ready branch (branch resolved through the same prefix)
$ FM_HOME=/tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/home bin/fm-review-diff.sh ship-demo-1 --stat
diff base: main
 feature.txt | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

## 4. Captain approves; firstmate lands the renamed branch into local main
$ FM_HOME=/tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/home bin/fm-merge-local.sh ship-demo-1
merged ardy/ship-demo-1 into local main (4396d35 -> 4388825) in /tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/project

$ git log --oneline -2    # project state after landing
4388825 ship the feature
4396d35 baseline

## 5. Invalid prefixes are refused loudly before anything is written
$ printf '%s\n' 'ardy/' > config/branch-prefix; bin/fm-brief.sh refuse-demo some-proj --mode local-only
error: /tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/home/config/branch-prefix must hold one line of letters, digits, and dashes with no slash (got 'ardy/')
(exit code 1; brief written: no)
$ printf '%s\n' '-ardy' > config/branch-prefix; bin/fm-brief.sh refuse-demo some-proj --mode local-only
error: /tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/home/config/branch-prefix must not start with a dash (got '-ardy'); git refuses such branch names
(exit code 1; brief written: no)
$ printf '%s\n' 'ar dy' > config/branch-prefix; bin/fm-brief.sh refuse-demo some-proj --mode local-only
error: /tmp/fmprefix/e2e2/home/config/branch-prefix must hold one line of letters, digits, and dashes with no slash (got 'ar dy')
(exit code 1; brief written: no)
(config restored to ardy; the next scaffold works again)
